.TH K2HVECLINETOOL "1" "September 2026" "K2HVECLINETOOL" "Vector database/search Library"
.SH NAME
K2HVECLINETOOL \- An interactive tool for managing and configuring K2HVEC databases.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B k2hveclinetool
[OPTIONS] [ \--help(-h) ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This is a command-line tool (interactive / command execution) for intuitively operating and testing database manipulations and vector searches.
It allows you to interactively operate and verify almost all features of the K2HVEC library, as well as execute commands automatically in batch mode by loading a command file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\--help(-h)\fR
Displays the help message for startup options
.TP
\fB\--library_version(-libver)\fR
Displays the versions of the K2HVEC library and related libraries
.TP
\fB\--history_max(-hmax)\fR <count>
Sets the maximum number of command history items retained in the prompt
.TP
\fB\--lap_time(-lap)\fR
Enables or disables the display of elapsed execution time for each command
.TP
\fB\--no_welcome_message(-no_welcome)\fR
Suppresses initial startup messages (such as banner text) when launching k2hveclinetool
.TP
\fB\--run_file(-run)\fR <file path>
Loads a command file containing prompt commands and executes them automatically in batch mode
.TP
\fB\--\fR <prompt commands...>
Executes the argument following this option directly as a prompt command
.TP
\fB\--file(-f)\fR <file path>
Specifies the path to the K2Hash database file used by the K2HVEC library
.TP
\fB\--temporary_file(-t)\fR
Uses an automatically deleted temporary file for the K2Hash database
.TP
\fB\--memory(-m)\fR
Constructs the K2Hash database in memory (In-Memory mode) for use by the K2HVEC library
.TP
\fB\--mask(-msk)\fR <bit count>
Specifies the number of mask bits used when creating the K2Hash database
.TP
\fB\--collision_mask(-cmask)\fR <bit count>
Specifies the number of collision mask (cmask) bits used when creating the K2Hash database
.TP
\fB\--element_count(-elcnt)\fR <count>
Specifies the initial element count used when creating the K2Hash database
.TP
\fB\--page_size(-page)\fR <size>
Specifies the page size used when creating the K2Hash database
.TP
\fB\--full_mapping(-full)\fR
Opens the K2Hash file (or memory) in full mapping mode (enabled by default for In-Memory mode; disabled by default for files)
.TP
\fB\--read_only(-r)\fR
Opens the K2Hash database in read-only mode
.TP
\fB\--debug_level(-d)\fR <debug mode>
Specifies the debug log output level (Allowed values: SILENT / SLT, ERROR / ERR, WARNING / WAN, MESSAGE / MSG, DUMP / DMP)
.TP
\fB\--debug_logfile(-dlog)\fR <file path>
Specifies the destination file path for debug log output (defaults to standard output/error if unspecified)
.TP
\fB\--binary_hash_bit_size(-bs)\fR <bit>
Specifies the number of bits for the calculated binary hash result
.TP
\fB\--neighbor_key_limit(-nkl)\fR <limit>
Specifies the maximum number of neighbor keys allowed for vector similarity searches
.TP
\fB\--content_direct_limit(-cdl)\fR <limit>
Specifies the maximum size for saving content text directly to the main key
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBVECDBGMODE\fR
VECDBGMODE environment sets debugging message level. The value is set as SILENT, ERR, WAN, INFO or DUMP.
When SIGUSER1 signal is caught, the debugging message level is bumpup. The level is changed as order by SILENT, ERR, WAN, INFO, DUMP, SILENT...
.TP
\fBVECDBGFILE\fR
VECDBGFILE environment sets the file which is debugging message.
